    narr:narration """A standing rule anchors this strata: [a composer's note records that nothing here exports to other sessions until the design is tested](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_4), and the framing for that rule sits in [an editorial lead-in to the quoted slowdown](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_5), spelled out directly in [the multi-sentence directive to slow down and finish the full design before ad hoc implementation](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_6). That gate is captured at the narrative level too, in [the cross-session build gate](narr:Narrative_CrossSessionBuildGate). A parallel thread presses toward reusing what already exists: [the shoulders-of-giants directive against rolling new components inside given constraints](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_43), generalized in [the extend-before-rolling-new narrative](narr:Narrative_ExtendExistingWork) and written down in [the extend-first rule record](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_45). A third concern narrows to output limits: [the circuit-breaker standard for caps, tripping only on runaway behavior rather than ordinary length](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_34), echoed in [the output-cap circuit-breaker narrative](narr:Narrative_OutputCapCircuitBreaker) and codified in [the llm-calls rule record](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_35). Underneath these rules sits a retrospective: [the assessment that reimplementing a database was a known mistake entered into by accident](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_41), and [the session's own accounting of which hand-rolled pieces were the weak link](narr:Expr_20261011_1_VerifyPr1031WrappingQuotesRepairOnDev_h2e601120d6cc_42).""" ;
